10
00:39:05,454 --> 00:39:11,454
The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn – Part 1 is a 2011 American vampire romantic fantasy film directed by Bill Condon
from a screenplay by Melissa Rosenberg, based on the 2008 novel Breaking Dawn by Stephenie Meyer.

11
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:06,000
It is the sequel to The Twilight Saga: Eclipse (2010) and the
fourth installment in The Twilight Saga film series.

12
00:46:54,545 --> 00:47:00,545
The film stars Kristen Stewart, Robert Pattinson, and Taylor Lautner, reprising their
roles as Bella Swan, Edward Cullen, and Jacob Black, respectively.

13
00:50:49,090 --> 00:50:55,090
In the film, Bella and Edward marry and become pregnant with a half-human, half-vampire child,
which causes the Cullen family to become a target of Jacob and his Wolf Pack.

14
00:54:43,636 --> 00:54:49,636
Summit Entertainment announced that Breaking Dawn would be
adapted into a two-part film on June 10, 2010.

15
00:58:38,181 --> 00:58:44,181
Principal photography for both parts began on November
1, 2010, and wrapped on April 22, 2011.

16
01:02:32,727 --> 01:02:38,727
The first part was shot in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil; Baton
Rouge, Louisiana; and Vancouver, Canada.

17
01:06:27,272 --> 01:06:33,272
The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn – Part 1 premiered at the Rome Film Festival on October 30, 2011, and
was theatrically released in the United States on November 18, by Summit Entertainment.

18
01:10:21,818 --> 01:10:27,818
The film received mixed to unfavorable reviews from critics with criticism aimed at pacing, screenplay and
performances, but grossed $732 million worldwide, becoming the fourth-highest-grossing film of 2011.

19
01:14:16,363 --> 01:14:22,363
A sequel, Breaking Dawn – Part 2, was released in 2012.

20
01:18:10,909 --> 01:18:16,909
The film explores themes of world war ii, prisoner of war, french resistance.

21
01:22:05,454 --> 01:22:11,454
The tone is intense.
